{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutValueKey","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A key for accessing a layout value of a layout container’s subviews."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LayoutValueKey"}],"role":"symbol","title":"LayoutValueKey","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LayoutValueKey","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI14LayoutValueKeyP","roleHeading":"Protocol","symbolKind":"protocol"},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Associated Types","anchor":"Associated-Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutValueKey\/Value"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutValueKey\/defaultValue"],"anchor":"Type-Properties"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LayoutValueKey"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you create a custom layout by defining a type that conforms to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" protocol, you can also create custom layout values"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that you set on individual views, and that your container view can access","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to guide its layout behavior. Your custom values resemble","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the built-in layout values that you set with view modifiers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"like ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/layoutPriority(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/zIndex(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but have a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"purpose that you define.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To create a custom layout value, define a type that conforms to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LayoutValueKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol and implement the one required property that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returns the default value of the property. For example, you can create","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a property that defines an amount of flexibility for a view, defined as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an optional floating point number with a default value of ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["private struct Flexibility: LayoutValueKey {","    static let defaultValue: CGFloat? = nil","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Swift compiler infers this particular key’s associated type as an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional ","type":"text"},{"text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/CoreFoundation\/CGFloat","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from this definition.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Set a value on a view","anchor":"Set-a-value-on-a-view"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Set the value on a view by adding the ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/layoutValue(key:value:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"view modifier to the view. To make your custom value easier to work","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with, you can do this in a convenience modifier in an extension of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/View","type":"reference"},{"text":" protocol:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["extension View {","    func layoutFlexibility(_ value: CGFloat?) -> some View {","        layoutValue(key: Flexibility.self, value: value)","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use your modifier to set the value on any views that need a nondefault","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["BasicVStack {","    Text(\"One View\")","    Text(\"Another View\")","        .layoutFlexibility(3)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Any view that you don’t explicitly set a value for uses the default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value, as with the first ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Text","type":"reference"},{"text":" view, above.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Retrieve a value during layout","anchor":"Retrieve-a-value-during-layout"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Access a custom layout value using the key as an index","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on subview’s proxy (an instance of ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview","type":"reference"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"and use the value to make decisions about sizing, placement, or other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"layout operations. For example, you might read the flexibility value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in your layout view’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview\/sizeThatFits(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"adjust your size calculations accordingly:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["extension BasicVStack {","    func sizeThatFits(","        proposal: ProposedViewSize,","        subviews: Subviews,","        cache: inout Void","    ) -> CGSize {","","        \/\/ Map the flexibility property of each subview into an array.","        let flexibilities = subviews.map { subview in","            subview[Flexibility.self]","        }","","        \/\/ Calculate and return the size of the layout container.","        \/\/ ...","    }","}"]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/layoutvaluekey"]}],"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/LayoutSubview/sizeThatFits(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/LayoutSubview\/sizeThatFits(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/layoutsubview\/sizethatfits(_:)","title":"sizeThatFits(_:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Asks the subview for its size."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sizeThatFits","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI16ProposedViewSizeV","text":"ProposedViewSize","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSpatial6Size3DV","text":"Size3D","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/LayoutSubview":{"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/layoutsubview","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LayoutSubview","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"LayoutSubview","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A proxy th